@startuml Transaction_State_Machine

title Transaction State Machine (from Customer.java, Transaction.java, Bank.java)

[*] --> Requested : customer.deposit() / withdraw() / transfer()

state "Validating" as Validating
Requested --> Validating : Transaction.validate(account, type, amount)

Validating --> COMPLETED : [amount > 0 and\nbalance - amount >= minimumBalance]\n/ account.withdraw() or deposit()\n/ log(..., "COMPLETED")

Validating --> FAILED : [amount <= 0 or\nbalance would drop below minimum]\n/ log(..., "FAILED")\n/ throw IllegalStateException

COMPLETED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

note bottom of COMPLETED
  Transaction is immutable.
  Status is fixed when it is created
  (withStatus() makes a new copy).
end note

note right of FAILED
  Bank.transfer(): if the deposit to the
  receiver fails, the sender is refunded.
end note

@enduml
